cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Market Ecology Simulator
message: >-
  An agent-based model of an equity market, validated against the
  stylized facts of real return series. If you use it, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: TjarkAI
repository-code: https://github.com/TjarkAI/market-ecology-simulator
abstract: >-
  Several hundred heterogeneous agents trade five sector instruments in a
  continuous double auction. No equation for the price exists anywhere in
  the model. The project asks whether such a population reproduces the
  statistical properties real return series share — fat tails, clustered
  volatility, a tail index between 2 and 6, near-zero return
  autocorrelation — when none of them are built in. Across 25 measurements
  four of six criteria hold, two of them in every measurement and two in 24
  and 22 of them; two fail, and the reason they fail is reported rather than
  tuned away.
keywords:
  - agent-based model
  - market microstructure
  - stylized facts
  - continuous double auction
  - computational finance
license: MIT
